DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvffss__ssuusseerr() function checks if the credentials given include supe‐
     ruser powers for the given mount point.  It will check to see if the
     thread passed in has the same credentials as the user that mounted the
     file system.  If so, it returns 0, otherwise it returns what
     priv_check(9) would have returned.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The vvffss__ssuusseerr() function returns 0 if the user has superuser powers and
     EPERM otherwise.  This is the _r_e_v_e_r_s_e _l_o_g_i_c of some other implementations
     of ssuusseerr() in which a TRUE response indicates superuser powers.

